From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corry K <blueblau@163.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] vllm-neuron framework changes for MiMo-V2.6-Flash

Changes to existing vllm-neuron modules that the MiMo-V2 model needs on the
PyTorch native backend:

- model registry, NeuronConfig fields and KV-cache groups for the hybrid
  sliding-window / global attention layout
- speculative decoding: MTP proposer, DFlash target-side support (auxiliary
  hidden states), verify-step positions and mixed speculative batches
- sampling aligned with GPU vLLM: top-p rule, per-request seed, logprobs,
  prompt_logprobs, penalties, logit_bias, greedy tie rule, host logits
  processing on verify steps
- structured outputs (grammar bitmask on the native route)
- scheduler: KV admission by the request's actual length, encoder-cache
  accounting for vision / audio items, block-aligned encoder cache manager
- MoE functional fixes (blockwise mapping, CTE token padding)
- model runner / worker: prefill buckets below the largest one, decode
  steps for large batches, batch-size pause of speculative steps,
  async-scheduler fix
- accuracy tooling (logit validation against FP32 references)
